#: ../../../deprecations/pending-removal-in-3.19.rst:2
msgid "Pending removal in Python 3.19"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecations/pending-removal-in-3.19.rst:4
msgid ":mod:`builtins`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecations/pending-removal-in-3.19.rst:6
msgid ""
"Passing a complex number as the *real* or *imag* argument in "
"the :func:`complex` constructor is now deprecated; it should only be passed "
"as a single positional argument. (Contributed by Serhiy Storchaka "
"in :gh:`109218`.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecations/pending-removal-in-3.19.rst:11
msgid ":mod:`ctypes`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecations/pending-removal-in-3.19.rst:13
msgid ""
"Implicitly switching to the MSVC-compatible struct layout by "
"setting :attr:`~ctypes.Structure._pack_` but "
"not :attr:`~ctypes.Structure._layout_` on non-Windows platforms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecations/pending-removal-in-3.19.rst:17
msgid ":mod:`hashlib`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecations/pending-removal-in-3.19.rst:19
msgid ""
"In hash function constructors such as :func:`~hashlib.new` or the direct "
"hash-named constructors such as :func:`~hashlib.md5` "
"and :func:`~hashlib.sha256`, their optional initial data parameter could "
"also be passed a keyword argument named ``data=`` or ``string=`` in "
"various :mod:`!hashlib` implementations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecations/pending-removal-in-3.19.rst:25
msgid ""
"Support for the ``string`` keyword argument name is now deprecated and "
"slated for removal in Python 3.19."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecations/pending-removal-in-3.19.rst:28
msgid ""
"Before Python 3.13, the ``string`` keyword parameter was not correctly "
"supported depending on the backend implementation of hash functions. Prefer "
"passing the initial data as a positional argument for maximum backwards "
"compatibility."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecations/pending-removal-in-3.19.rst:33
msgid ":mod:`http.cookies`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecations/pending-removal-in-3.19.rst:35
msgid ""
":meth:`http.cookies.Morsel.js_output` is deprecated and will be removed in "
"Python 3.19."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecations/pending-removal-in-3.19.rst:38
msgid ""
":meth:`http.cookies.BaseCookie.js_output` is deprecated and will be removed "
"in Python 3.19."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecations/pending-removal-in-3.19.rst:41
msgid ":mod:`imaplib`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecations/pending-removal-in-3.19.rst:43
msgid ""
"Altering :attr:`IMAP4.file <imaplib.IMAP4.file>` is now deprecated and "
"slated for removal in Python 3.19. This property is now unused and changing "
"its value does not automatically close the current file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecations/pending-removal-in-3.19.rst:47
msgid ""
"Before Python 3.14, this property was used to implement the corresponding "
"``read()`` and ``readline()`` methods for :class:`~imaplib.IMAP4` but this "
"is no longer the case since then."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecations/pending-removal-in-3.19.rst:51
msgid ":mod:`tkinter`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecations/pending-removal-in-3.19.rst:53
msgid ""
":func:`tkinter.filedialog.askopenfiles` has been deprecated since Python "
"3.16.  Iterate over the names returned "
"by :func:`~tkinter.filedialog.askopenfilenames` and open them one by one "
"instead. (Contributed by Serhiy Storchaka in :gh:`152638`.)"
msgstr ""
